    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 score makes him our clear anchor. Facing a favorable matchup against a 4.41 xERA arm, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite park factor and a significant platoon edge, cementing his status as the primary offensive engine. We also see substantial value from **Drake Baldwin** (71.83) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.56). **Drake Baldwin** is thriving in the leadoff spot with favorable park conditions, while **Jackson Merrill** leverages a robust 14% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill set to overcome a slight park disadvantage, making both high-priority starts.\n\nOur tactical lineup management hinges on maximizing efficiency, which led to a difficult bench decision regarding **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (47.58). While he was a strong candidate, the optimizer ultimately favored the higher-floor projections of **Dominic Smith** (62.63) and **Andy Pages** (60.70). **Dominic Smith** is bolstered by an excellent park factor, while **Andy Pages** retains utility value despite the negative impact of facing an elite-tier catcher behind the plate. We have opted to keep **Brayan Rocchio** (36.60) on the bench entirely, as his efficiency rating fell below our 40-point threshold, signaling that his current matchup provides insufficient ROI for our limited game cap allotment.\n\nInvestors should remain mindful of the risk profile surrounding **Heliot Ramos** (52.48). While he is a capable talent, the combination of a tough opposing pitcher and the inherent drag of the elite-hold catcher dynamic currently restricts his ceiling. Furthermore, we are monitoring the lineup status of several key bats; should any of our projected leadoff hitters like **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, or **Sam Antonacci** slide down the order upon final confirmation, we may see a volatility shift in their respective scores. For now, the roster remains set to capitalize on our core power hitters and speed threats, aiming to maintain our standing in the 5x5 rotation.",
